<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Clandeboye O'Neills</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Clann Aodha Buidhe</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Clandeboye O'Neills, in Irish Clann Aodha Buidhe, were a branch of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/o-neill-dynasty">O'Neill dynasty</a> of Tyrone that crossed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/river-bann">River Bann</a> in the 14th century. They took over much of south Antrim and north Down from the declining earldom of Ulster and formed the lordship of Clandeboye. Their power ended in the early 17th century, when their last lord, Con O'Neill, lost most of his lands to Scottish settlers.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/clandeboye-oneills.jpg" alt="Clandeboye O'Neills" width="320" height="267" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mabuska · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ulster_Early_16th_Century.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
